      "message": "Do you think it would be better to have the following structure?\n\n```\n  // Add \"serialized\" to the function names\n  void setSerializedAgtm(sk_sp\u003cSkData\u003e);\n  sk_sp\u003cSkData\u003e getSerializedAgtm() const;\n\n  // Maybe in the future add this getter, which just wraps\n  // Agtm::Make(getSerializedAgtm().get())\n  std::unique_ptr\u003cAgtm\u003e getAgtm() const;\n```\n\nI also wonder about the above MDCV and CLLI interfaces. Maybe it would be a good idea to expose the same interface for them as well (so they would return an `std::unique_ptr` instead of the current `bool`-based accessor).",
