      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, so your general idea is to have Metadata be a \"box of bytes\" and then clients can get/set the bytes for each section? And if they want to parse it, they call the above? I think that\u0027s ok, but maybe it\u0027s convenient to also have\n```\n  void setSerializedAgtm(sk_sp\u003cconst SkData\u003e);\n  sk_sp\u003cconst SkData\u003e getSerializedAgtm() const;\n  std::unique_ptr\u003cAgtm\u003e getAgtm() const {\n     return Agtm::Make(fAgtm);\n  }\n```\nor call that last thing `parseAgtm()` to indicate it\u0027s not a simple getter.\n\nThe \"serialized\" in the name is good. Can use `sk_sp\u003cconst SkData\u003e` on both of these? I think we want to tell people \"we promise not to touch the data as we parse it\". Because we are caching the serialized data, I\u0027d want to return a `sk_sp\u003cconst SkData\u003e` to tell people not to mess with it.",
